35,2,1,talk,May,,"The ferry trial worked, but the rail and ferry data terms were never agreed.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The late-turn pool is gone. Overtime is covering everything.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Audits show waiting for connections is the real time sink, not ticketing.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The pre-war shells have hidden voids. Bidders are pricing heavy contingency.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The capital ledger has a ring-fenced balance, but operating funds are trimmed.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, does that mean station work is risky?","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, if data terms aren't agreed, how do we integrate fares?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, if crews are thin, night service is impossible.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, can we use that ring-fenced balance for anything?","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the maintenance contract has spare capacity for lifts, though.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,The committee minutes confirm the data gap. That blocks integration.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The crew establishment is a third below target. We can't promise new routes.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"The mid-city runs are slower, but platforms clear fine. Bus corridors might help.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"The contingency costs are high, but the accessibility records show some success.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The ticketing fees are high, but the paving rates are climbing too.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"So, integration is blocked by data, and night service is blocked by staff.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. We need a plan that fits our current capacity.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,A bus corridor uses existing crews and addresses the mid-city delay.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"Station upgrades are risky due to the shells, but the lift contract has slack.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"The budget supports targeted fixes, not massive new systems.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
